<!--Post: 8533--><!--Time: 1109187405-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8533"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 11:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->First, the Thomas-Kilmann webage you refer to is a single page referencing the Thomas Kilmann Conflict Mode Intrument created by Kenneth Thomas and Ralph Kilmann. The TKI is referenced on thousands of internet sites and literally hundreds of equivalent team training and personality profile web sites. <BR> <BR>I could find no place in the personal history of any of these men a reference to having lived in or around Wichita Kansas. <BR> <BR>The fact that they were all around 15-18 years of age in 1974 seems to have escaped your investigation as well.  <BR> <BR>Why does the fact that one of them lived in Germany for 16 years and then Japan for 2 make him or one of the others a POI? <BR> <BR>If you have anything other than ZOMG one of them looks like an aged sketch of what BTK might look like, please provide it. <BR> <BR>I assume you are pointing to these facts so I will spell them out for you. <BR> <BR>Brian is a member of Mensa. <BR>Brian has a rather photographic memory, having memorized 1000 digits of pi. <BR>Brian is married to a woman named Petra. <BR> <BR>Things that go against it.  <BR> <BR>Except for Brian only Mick Calvacca lived outside of the New York/ New Jersey area &#40;Connecticut and Florida&#41;.  <BR> <BR>In 1974 most of them went off to college. Brian went to Cornell &#40;in New York&#41;. 3 years later he left for Germany in 1977 where he remained for 16 years. <BR> <BR>Calling this a long shot is a dramatic overstatement.  <BR> <BR>Ron <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8533-->
<!--Post: 8596--><!--Time: 1109219084-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8596"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 8:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Half the crimes were committed in March/April... the rest in December/January... Spring/Christmas break? <BR> <BR>Was 2 in Germany, the rest in Japan. <BR> <BR>The group traveled from New York to California. With maybe Kansas in-between? <BR> <BR>I did not say check the sketch. I said check the sketches. <BR> <BR>:|<!--/Text--></td></tr>
